00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.490
You may recall that Paul
Manafort was indicted

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.360
in two separate jurisdictions.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.310
He was the defendant in one
particular criminal case

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.020
on the Eastern District of
Virginia, that's federal court,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.300
as well as the District of D.C.,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.260
which again is another federal district.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.321
The Eastern District of Virginia,

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:13.590
because of its proximity to D.C.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.720
Handles a lot of very
high profile federal cases

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.730
and this is no exception to that.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.950
The Virginia case went to trial first.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.490
Paul Manafort was convicted
on most of the crimes alleged

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.840
in the Eastern District of Virginia case,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.500
and the jury hung on
a few of those claims,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.450
meaning they weren't able to
come to a unanimous decision

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.170
on those particular claims.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.090
As a result of losing
so many of the claims

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.670
in the Virginia case,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.690
enough to put him away
for the rest of his life,

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.820
Manafort and his legal team
decided to plead out in D.C.,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.220
meaning he took a plea agreement

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.910
where he got a reduced
sentence in exchange

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.600
for him cooperating with the
ongoing Mueller investigation.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.260
Not surprisingly, the plea agreement

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.339
that Mueller and Manafort entered into

00:01:55.339 --> 00:01:58.960
requires that Manafort cooperate entirely

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.560
not only into the actual crimes

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.280
that he was indicted and convicted of

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.420
but also for any investigations

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.420
that Mueller wants his cooperation with

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.490
and that Manafort might
have some information

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.620
that would help out.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.480
Manafort pleaded pursuant to an agreement

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.170
that required his fully,
truthfully, completely,

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.520
and forthrightly cooperating
with the government.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.260
According to the sentencing memo

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.140
that the Mueller team just filed,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.760
the plea agreement provides
that if the defendant,

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.440
Manafort, fails to fulfill completely

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.600
each and every one of his obligations

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.497
under the plea agreement or quote,

00:02:32.497 --> 00:02:36.160
"engages in any criminal
activity prior to sentencing,"

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.200
the defendant, Manafort, will
be in breach of the agreement.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.570
And, of course, a breach
relieves the government

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.750
of any obligations
under the plea agreement

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.480
including its agreement to a reduction

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.840
of the sentencing
guidelines for acceptance

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.060
and responsibility but leaves intact

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.770
all of the obligations of the defendant

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.030
as well as his guilty pleas.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.230
Which means that if Manafort
violated the plea agreement

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:02.180
he is not entitled to any
reduction of any of the crimes

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.870
that he was convicted of an
in fact he cannot withdraw

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.790
his guilty plea as a result.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.870
No matter what, Manafort
is going to be stuck

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.040
with his admission of guilt
with no reduction in sentence.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.690
In the status report that the
Mueller team recently filed

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.870
both in D.C. and Virginia,
according to Mueller,

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.300
after signing the plea agreement,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.800
Manafort committed federal crimes by lying

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.512
to the Federal Bureau of Investigation

00:03:24.512 --> 00:03:26.410
and the Special Counsel's Office

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.140
on a variety of subject matters

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.570
which constitute breaches
of the agreement.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.370
The government will file a
detailed sentencing submission

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.020
to the probation department

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.720
and the Court in advance of
the sentencing that sets forth

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.700
the nature of the
defendant's crimes and lies

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.830
including those after signing
the plea agreement herein.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.890
This is a bombshell filing
by the Mueller team.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.460
It is very rare for these
kinds of plea agreements

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.360
to blow up and what the
Mueller team has hinted at here

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.128
is that Manafort not only just lied once

00:03:56.128 --> 00:03:57.730
and failed to communicate

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.564
but lied on a variety
of different subjects.

00:04:00.564 --> 00:04:02.400
So what are the consequences

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.320
of this plea agreement blowing up?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.850
Well for one the Mueller team

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.870
won't be able to use Paul
Manafort as a cooperating witness.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.030
They won't be able to rely
on his testimony at trial.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.640
They won't get him to waive
his 5th Amendment rights

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.070
against self incrimination

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.950
and of course Paul
Manafort is going to jail

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.530
for a very, very long time.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.740
The reason you enter into
one of these plea agreements

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.830
is to get a reduction in your sentence.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.850
You make it easier for the
government to prove their case,

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.830
you admit your guilt, and in exchange

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.750
the government gives you a letter

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.150
saying that you should get
a reduction in sentence.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.117
A judge has some leeway in what sentence

00:04:35.117 --> 00:04:36.751
is actually handed down.

00:04:36.751 --> 00:04:39.740
There are federal guidelines,
federal sentencing guidelines

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.410
that provide a certain range

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.240
and the judge is allowed to
choose from within that range

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.400
and the government states

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.426
that because you cooperated
with their investigation

00:04:47.426 --> 00:04:49.860
you should get a
reduction in your sentence

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.314
at the low end of the
sentencing guideline range.

00:04:52.314 --> 00:04:55.421
Of course, when you back out
of a plea agreement like this

00:04:55.421 --> 00:04:58.280
the government no longer needs
to say nice things about you

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.500
and no longer needs to argue

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.660
that you should get a
reduction in your sentence

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.780
and in fact they will
do exactly the opposite.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.490
Instead, the government will argue

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.714
that because of your bad conduct

00:05:06.714 --> 00:05:09.900
you should get an
enhancement in your sentence.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.700
You should be at the high end of the range

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.463
or if you engaged in new crimes,

00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:17.390
then you can be sentenced
to additional time

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.410
that was not reflected in
your original guilty plea.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.700
So Paul Manafort is in a world of hurt.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.250
Manafort's breach of the plea agreement

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.970
and lies to federal prosecutors

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.130
may be related to a report coming out

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.000
of the UK's Guardian Newspaper

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.050
which reports that Paul
Manafort met extensively

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:37.260
with Julian Assange of WikiLeaks
before the 2016 election.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.740
If that is proved to be true,

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.998
that could have huge implications

00:05:40.998 --> 00:05:43.680
for the conspiracy and
collusion investigation

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.580
that's going on.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.179
On top of that, there
is yet another bombshell

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:49.970
that reports that while
Manafort was acting

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:52.820
as a cooperating witness
with the Mueller team,

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:54.681
both Manafort and his attorneys

00:05:54.681 --> 00:05:58.510
were passing secret
information to President Trump

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.360
and the other Trump campaign defendants.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.251
This is a huge bombshell.

00:06:04.251 --> 00:06:06.940
Generally speaking, if
you talk to your lawyer,

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.650
those communications are protected

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.910
by attorney-client
privilege, no surprise there.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.780
If you talk to a third party
who is not your attorney,

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.090
the general rule is

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.720
there is no attorney-client
privilege whatsoever.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.500
Those communications are not privileged

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.040
and they are discoverable.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.130
However, when you have multiple
defendants on one side,

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:28.130
often they share what's
called a common interest.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.380
Which means that what's
good for one defendant

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.410
is also good for the other
defendants and as a result

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.550
it's very favorable to be
able to share information

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.880
among different defendants
and their lawyers.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.570
And you wouldn't wanna
share that information

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.770
if it breached attorney-client privilege

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.520
and those communications were exposed.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.660
So the court recognizes

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.930
what's called a common interest doctrine,

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.180
which allows those defendants
to communicate back and forth.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.600
To do that you have to sign

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.490
what's called a Joint Defense Agreement

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:57.690
which basically just
codifies that relationship

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.380
and allows communications
to go back and forth.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.465
However, the wrinkle comes

00:07:01.465 --> 00:07:04.404
when one of those
defendants no longer shares

00:07:04.404 --> 00:07:06.980
a common interest with
the other defendants.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:10.310
When one of those defendants
enters into a plea agreement

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.390
that defendant's interests

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.330
are no longer aligned
with the other defendants.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.450
The other defendants
presumably wanna fight the case

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.970
and wanna be proven innocent

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.490
whereas the defendant who has pled guilty

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:22.910
wants a reduction in sentence

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:25.190
and wants to make the prosecution's case

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.540
as easy as possible.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.130
So in that circumstance, those defendants

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.100
are no longer in the same common interest.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.490
So what generally happens

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.240
is that when one defendant pleads out

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.680
they remove themselves from
the Joint Defense Agreement

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.290
so that their communications
are not exposed

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.720
and discoverable and the other
defendants' communications

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.890
are no longer exposed and discoverable.

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:48.940
But apparently that did not happen here,

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:52.010
even after Manafort entered
into his plea agreement,

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.030
was a cooperating witness
with the Mueller team,

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.640
and had pled guilty to the crimes alleged

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.990
in the District of Columbia case,

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.700
he was still part of the
Joint Defense Agreement

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.960
with the rest of the Trump team.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.214
That means that the communications

00:08:05.214 --> 00:08:08.124
that any of the Trump lawyers
and Trump defendants had

00:08:08.124 --> 00:08:11.020
with Manafort or his attorneys,

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.420
while under the guise of
this Joint Defense Agreement

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.120
are no longer protected.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.290
If those communications
and that work product

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.120
is no longer protected by
the Joint Defense Agreement

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.745
and no longer protected by
the attorney-client privilege

00:08:23.745 --> 00:08:26.210
then they are discoverable.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.190
If I was one of Mueller's investigators

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.240
I would simply send a written request over

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.130
to not only Paul Manafort's lawyers

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.940
but to all of the Trump defendant lawyers

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.250
demanding that they turn
over any communications

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.866
and any work product that
was shared amongst themselves

00:08:40.866 --> 00:08:44.210
while Paul Manafort was
a cooperating witness.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.640
Because Paul Manafort doesn't
have the same interest

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.010
as the rest of the defendants
and potential defendants

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:51.950
in this investigation, the
Common Interest doctrine

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.920
doesn't apply and the
Joint Defense Agreement

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.730
can't protect all of their communications

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:57.770
and their work product.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.400
Not only does this have
malpractice written all over it

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.200
if the clients weren't
apprised of the fact

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.410
that they could be subject
to these disclosures

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.680
as a result of these
secret communications,

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:07.840
but on top of that

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.770
I don't think that Paul Manafort's lawyers

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.520
are really going to be able to practice

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:12.910
in federal court anymore

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:16.160
because no prosecutor
would ever trust them

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.170
to keep the terms of a
plea agreement secret.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.788
And if you can't negotiate
with the government

00:09:21.788 --> 00:09:25.390
then your value as a federal
criminal defense lawyer

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.320
is really going to plummet.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.830
So why would someone do this?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.170
Well, a lot of people are speculating

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.030
that Paul Manafort is angling
for a Presidential pardon

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.540
and that may be true.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.480
There are two schools of thought here.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.160
The first is that Paul Manafort

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.520
thinks he is the smartest guy in the room

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:43.010
and he can beat the federal prosecutors.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:43.970
It's not uncommon

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.430
for criminals to think that
they are smarter than they are

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:47.960
and smarter than the prosecutors

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.760
who are going to put them in jail,

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:51.910
especially when it comes
to white collar criminals

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.470
like Paul Manafort who
are used to getting away

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.860
with skirting the law
and beating regulators.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:57.693
So it may be

00:09:57.693 --> 00:09:59.620
that Manafort just thinks
he can get away with it.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.370
He lied his way into the situation

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.360
and he can lie his way out
of the situation, we'll see.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.640
The second school of thought on this

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.886
is that Manafort is angling
for a Presidential pardon.

00:10:08.886 --> 00:10:12.380
If he works with Mueller he
can get a reduction in sentence

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:15.180
but the theory is that if he
works with President Trump

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.070
who can pardon him, he
can avoid jail altogether.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.650
That could be, but there
are some problems with that

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:24.150
because remember Manafort has been charged

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.100
in both Virginia and D.C.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.629
and there have been credible reports

00:10:27.629 --> 00:10:30.320
that Manafort is guilty
of all kinds of crimes

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.800
in New York as well.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:33.151
And the problem for Manafort

00:10:33.151 --> 00:10:35.181
is that a lot of the same conduct

00:10:35.181 --> 00:10:38.230
for which he has already pled guilty

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.470
could give rise to state-level charges.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:43.680
Specifically in the case
of Virginia and New York,

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.500
he could be convicted of tax fraud.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.510
And remember, a Presidential pardon

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.470
can only pardon federal crimes.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:54.120
Which would still leave
Manafort on the hook

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.990
for any state law crimes.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:56.823
On top of that

00:10:56.823 --> 00:10:58.896
the Mueller team is probably
going to retry Manafort

00:10:58.896 --> 00:11:02.740
on all of the crimes for which
the jury hung in Virginia

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:05.316
and they will argue for an
enhancement of sentencing

00:11:05.316 --> 00:11:08.830
for the crimes that Manafort
has already pled guilty.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.470
In the latest status report,
the Mueller team has promised

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.210
to lay out all of
Manafort's lies and failures

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.900
to cooperate in great detail.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.350
It's going to be fascinating
